TITLE:: FSWasp
summary:: Virtual Analog Model of the Electronic Dream Plant (EDP) Wasp VCF
categories:: UGens>Filters
related:: Classes/MS20Diode, Classes/MS20Circuit, Classes/MS20OTA

DESCRIPTION::
FSWasp is a virtual analog model of the distinctive state-variable filter (VCF) from the Electronic Dream Plant (EDP) Wasp synthesizer (1978).

The circuit uses CA3080 operational transconductance amplifiers (OTAs) as controllable integrators and CD4069 unbuffered CMOS inverters as summing nodes and inverting amplifiers.

This model is derived from the circuit analysis and measurement data published by L. Köper, M. Holters, F. Esqueda, and J. D. Parker (DAFx 2022). It includes both the analytical resonance network damping transfer function and the nonlinear transfer characteristics of the CA3080 OTA differential input stage (tanh saturation) and CD4069 CMOS inverter soft clipping solved via a fast implicit 1-D Newton-Raphson iteration.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: ar

ARGUMENT:: in
Audio-rate input signal.

ARGUMENT:: freq
Filter cutoff frequency in Hertz (10 Hz to 0.49 * sampleRate). Supports audio rate and control rate.

ARGUMENT:: res
Resonance parameter in [0.0, 1.0], mapping to the physical potentiometer network travel.

ARGUMENT:: drive
Overdrive factor (default 1.0, range [0.0, 20.0]).
When set to 0.0, runs the pure linear small-signal model.
When set > 0.0, runs the nonlinear model with OTA differential saturation and CMOS inverter compression.

ARGUMENT:: mode
Filter mode selection (integer, init-only):
TABLE::
## 0 || Low-Pass (12 dB/octave)
## 1 || Band-Pass (6 dB/octave skirt, symmetric peak)
## 2 || High-Pass (12 dB/octave)
::

returns:: An audio-rate filtered signal.

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
// Boot server
s.boot;

// 1. Low-Pass sweep with saw oscillator
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.5]) * 0.2;
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.2).exprange(100, 8000);
    FSWasp.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: 0.6, drive: 1.0, mode: 0) * 0.3;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 2. Band-Pass noise sweep with high resonance
(
x = {
    var src = PinkNoise.ar(0.3 ! 2);
    var cutoff = SinOsc.kr(0.15).exprange(200, 4000);
    var res = Line.kr(0.1, 0.95, 4);
    FSWasp.ar(src, freq: cutoff, res: res, drive: 1.0, mode: 1) * 0.25;
}.play;
)
x.free;

// 3. Nonlinear Overdrive Sweep (drive from 1.0 to 6.0)
(
x = {
    var src = Saw.ar([110, 110.2]) * 0.3;
    var drive = Line.kr(1.0, 6.0, 5);
    FSWasp.ar(src, freq: 1200, res: 0.7, drive: drive, mode: 0) * 0.25;
}.play;
)
x.free;
::
